**Embed slot: nomic-embed-text-v2-moe for default/high, v1.5 for low/cpu**

The v2-moe is a sparse MoE embedding model — better MTEB scores than v1.5 at a similar or smaller memory footprint. It has an official GGUF repo from nomic-ai. The v1.5 fallback for low-memory and CPU profiles is because v2-moe's MoE architecture benefits more from GPU and the quality gap closes on the GGUF Q4 variants anyway. Both use 768-dimensional embeddings, so your index schema doesn't change across profiles — a meaningful implementation simplification.

**Why not Qwen3.5?**

Qwen3.5 small models (0.8B, 2B, 4B, 9B) were released very recently and the bartowski quantizations exist, but the official Alibaba GGUF repos haven't stabilized for all sizes yet, and community testing is thin. For a product shipping to non-technical users, "newer" is not the same as "better-tested." Use Qwen3 now, add a `[profiles.*.upgrade_to]` field to models.toml so a manifest update can migrate users later without code changes.

